Z||000000||Bill H||01-16-2001||08:20 PM||||I know that this has been asked before but what has better heads, fiero 2.8 or gm performance 3.4. I want to have my heads ported and polished but am not sure to use the old 2.8 heads or the new heads off the 3.4.  Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||dman||01-17-2001||05:41 PM||||Hello Bill. I'm surprised no one has answered your question yet. I believe they are the same heads. The valve sizes are the same. The only thing that I've heard might be different would be the springs (though I don't remember where I heard that so I wouldn't be too sure about that).<P>Take all of this with caution since I haven't compared my 3.4 heads with my 2.8 heads. I'd give Terry or George a call at the fieroshop to be sure.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||01-17-2001||06:50 PM||||I have heads form the 3.4-liter OHV engine and my 2.8-liter engine and they are the same heads. I am using the 2.8 heads on my 3.4-liter engine only because I ported the 2.8 heads before I got a good 3.4-liter engine. I don't know about the springs though so you should use the 3.4-liter heads if you are keeping the same camshaft otherwise it doesn’t matter.||||reg||1
